10 REM KALEIDOSCOPE - MACHINE CODE DRAWS, BASIC ASKS
20 REM BLOCK AT 768, PARAMETERS IN ITS FIRST THREE BYTES, ENTRY CALL 771
30 TEXT
40 CALL -936
50 INPUT "SEED (0-255)",S
60 INPUT "TWIST (0-255)",T
70 INPUT "PASSES (1-9)",N
80 IF N<1 THEN N=1
90 IF N>9 THEN N=9
100 POKE 768,ABS(S) MOD 256
110 POKE 769,ABS(T) MOD 256
120 POKE 770,N
130 REM GR CLEARS THE LO-RES PAGE, WHICH IS THE SAME MEMORY THE PROMPTS USED
140 GR
150 CALL 771
160 REM PEEK(-16384) IS THE WAIT: A KEY DOES NOT STOP A PROGRAM ON THIS MACHINE
170 K=PEEK(-16384)
180 IF K<128 THEN 170
190 POKE -16368,0
200 GOTO 30
